{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cfun78nYipcsMPQBWuktK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"When the Cloudflare Agents MCP client (`MCPClientManager`, which wraps the official `@modelcontextprotocol/sdk` `Client`) connects to a server, the first protocol message it sends is a JSON-RPC **`initialize` request**. That request carries the client's supported `protocolVersion`, its `capabilities`, and `clientInfo` (name/version). After the server returns its own capabilities and server info, the client sends a **`notifications/initialized`** notification. Only then does it make discovery calls such as `tools/list`, `prompts/list` and `resources/list`.\n\nAt the transport level, the details vary. With the Streamable HTTP transport, the `initialize` message is sent as an HTTP POST. With the legacy SSE transport, the client first opens a GET event stream and then POSTs `initialize`. If the server requires OAuth, the client may also go through an auth redirect before the handshake completes.\n\nI answered this from my knowledge of the SDK and didn't check the source in this session."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2247,"cache_read_input_tokens":535,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2247},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"136dcf17-c80b-4627-8edc-f3ea3f05deb8","uuid":"e77fae8b-cbae-4d2a-8953-fbc58a59c6a0","timestamp":"2026-10-11T03:57:56.173Z","request_id":"req_011Cfun78a8tjdXkZdTHjbwd"}
